  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka has officially submitted a formal resignation letter to the People's Consultative Assembly of Indonesia.",
    "The official departure follows a meeting with President Prabowo Subianto, who reportedly accepted the decision with reluctance.",
    "Political reactions remain mixed, with some officials viewing the resignation as a statesmanship gesture, while others suggest it aims to avoid impeachment."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 12, 2026, Indonesian Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka formally resigned from his position, submitting his official letter to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR). Following the submission, he departed the Vice Presidential Palace after expressing gratitude toward President Prabowo Subianto and offering an apology to the public. The move has triggered significant national attention, with the Golkar faction within the MPR characterizing the resignation as an act of statesmanship. Conversely, the PDIP faction in North Sumatra has alleged that the resignation serves as a tactical maneuver to circumvent potential impeachment proceedings. The political developments coincided with notable volatility in financial markets, where the Indonesian Rupiah reached a record low. The resignation concludes a three-day period of intense political activity leading up to the official confirmation of his exit from the vice presidency.",
